{{also|Deviant|déviant}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|devyaunt|t=deviating, different}}, from {{der|en|LL.|dēviāns}}, present participle of {{m|la|dēviō|t=to stray, deviate or detour}}.<ref name="Etymonline">{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary|pos=adj|v=8482}}</ref><ref name="MED">{{R:MED Online|entry=dēviaunt|pos=''adj.'' and ''n.''|noformat=1|id=MED11475}}</ref><ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=adj|id=1441037424}}</ref> The noun is from the adjective, possibly attested in Middle English with the meaning “one who goes astray”.<ref name="Etymonline"/><ref name="MED"/><ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=4893852933}}</ref>
* {{sense|DeviantArt member}} So called because the website was originally for people who [[modify|modified]] (deviated) computer [[application]]s.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈdiː.vi.ənt/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-deviant.wav|a=UK}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Characterized by deviation from an [[expectation]] or a [[social]] [[standard]].
#: {{ux|en|At the trial, the extent of his '''deviant''' behavior became clear.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=2019-05-01|url=https://www.nathanrabin.com/happy-place/2019/5/1/my-world-of-flops-get-a-load-of-this-maroon-case-file-121my-year-of-flops-16-jacob-wohl|title=My World of Flops Get a Load of This Maroon Case File #121/My Year of Flops # 18 Jacob Wohl|text=He’s like more successful but equally morally abhorrent right-wing undercover operative James O’Keefe’s non-union Mexican equivalent, a dunce whose one move involves incompetently attempting to frame figures of seemingly unimpeachable moral integrity, like Robert Mueller or good old Mayor Pete, as '''deviant''' sex criminals like Wohl’s God Donald Trump by unsuccessfully trying to get people to come forward with bogus sexual assault allegations.|site=Nathan Rabin's Happy Place|author={{w|Nathan Rabin}}}}

